":["We'll be initially loading 500,000 records rather that loading the entire dataset (which has almost 42M records). \n","\n","Rather than randomly sampling individual records, sampling by user_id or user_session would allow me to preserve the relationships between events and understand the complete customer journey: \n","\n","**View → Add to Cart → Purchase.**"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"acaad397","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002589,"end_time":"2026-11-22T14:11:37.384623+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-22T14:11:37.382034+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["Since we have 9.24 million unique user session IDs, if we take 5% of that, it would give us approximately 462,000 sessions. \n","Reading 9.24 million user session IDs and randomly sampling 5% of that would waste a lot of time and RAM.\n","\n","The workaround? -> Hashing the session IDs\n","\n","The same session ID will always produce the same hash value.\n","\n","*So, how do we select the 5%?* \n","We use the below rule.\n","\n","```{python}\n","hash_value % 20 == 0\n","```\n","\n","This means:\n","- Calculate the hash value of a session ID.\n","- Divide it by 20.\n","- If the remainder is 0, keep that session.\n","- Otherwise, discard it.\n","\n","*Why 20?* Because approximately 1 out of every 20 hash values will satisfy this condition.\n","\n","**That's approximately 5%!**\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"id":"0fa84869","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-22T14:11:37.391952Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-22T14:11:37.391391Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-22T14:11:37.397268Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-22T14:11:37.396327Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.012068,"end_time":"2026-11-22T14:11:37.399295+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-22T14:11:37.387227+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["file_path = r\"/kaggle/input/datasets/mkechinov/ecommerce-behavior-data-from-multi-category-store/2019-Oct.csv\"\n","\n","cols_to_use = [\"user_id\",\n","               \"event_time\",\n","               \"event_type\", \n","               \"brand\", \n","               \"price\",\n","               \"category_code\", \n","               \"user_session\",\n","               \"product_id\"]\n","chunksize = 500_000\n","# rng = np.random.default_rng(42)  # reproducible random sampling\n","\n","sample_rate = 0.05  # e.g., 5% of sessions\n","threshold = int(sample_rate * (2**32))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"34537109","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-22T14:11:37.408338Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-22T14:11:37.407343Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-22T14:14:23.447717Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-22T14:14:23.446465Z"},"papermill":{"duration":166.048536,"end_time":"2026-11-22T14:14:23.450626+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-22T14:11:37.40209+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def in_session_sample(session_series: pd.Series) -> pd.Series:\n","    # Initial check to see whether the sample rate is between 0 and 1\n","    if sample_rate <= 0:\n","        return pd.Series(False, index=session_series.index)\n","    if sample_rate >= 1:\n","        return session_series.notna()\n","\n","    hashes = session_series.fillna(\"\").map( # Replaces missing session IDs with empty strings.\n","        lambda s: zlib.crc32(s.encode(\"utf-8\")) # Converts the session ID into a numerical hash.\n","        if s else 2**32\n","    )\n","    return hashes < threshold\n","\n","# def in_session_sample(session_series: pd.Series) -> pd.Series:\n","#     hashes = session_series.fillna(\"\").map( # Replaces missing session IDs with empty strings.\n","#         lambda s: zlib.crc32(s.encode(\"utf-8\")) # Converts the session ID into a numerical hash.\n","#         if s else 2**32 \n","#     )\n","#     return hashes % 20 == 0 #Checks whether the hash is divisible by 20.\n","\n","\n","reader = pd.read_csv(file_path, usecols=cols_to_use, chunksize=chunksize)\n","writer = None\n","\n","\n","# For every chunk:\n","# 1. Check whether the event is view, cart, or purchase.\n","# 2. Check whether its session ID passes the 5% hash rule.\n","# 3. Keep the row only if both conditions are satisfied.\n","\n","for chunk in reader:\n","    mask = (\n","        chunk[\"event_type\"].isin([\"view\", \"cart\", \"purchase\"]) # core events in the funnel cycle\n","        & in_session_sample(chunk[\"user_session\"]) # only focussing on the user session column for now\n","    )\n","    chunk = chunk[mask].copy()\n","\n","    if chunk.empty:\n","        continue\n","\n","    # Parse the timestamps and assigning appropriate data types to columns\n","    chunk[\"event_time\"] = pd.to_datetime(chunk[\"event_time\"], errors=\"coerce\") \n","    chunk[\"event_type\"] = chunk[\"event_type\"].astype(\"category\")\n","    if chunk[\"price\"].dtype == \"float64\":\n","        chunk[\"price\"] = chunk[\"price\"].astype(\"float32\")\n","\n","    # Converts the current Pandas chunk into an Apache Arrow Table\n","    # (the in-memory columnar format PyArrow uses to write Parquet files)\n","    table = pa.Table.from_pandas(chunk, preserve_index=False)\n","    if writer is None:\n","        writer = pq.ParquetWriter(\"Oct_500K_sample.parquet\", table.schema, compression=\"snappy\")\n","    writer.write_table(table)\n","\n","if writer is not None:\n","    writer.close()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"9c15e5f2","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002724,"end_time":"2026-11-22T14:14:23.456541+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-22T14:14:23.453817+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Data Cleaning and Preprocessing"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"05687477","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002676,"end_time":"2026-11-22T14:14:23.461918+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-22T14:14:23.459242+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Understanding the Data"]},{"cell_